; A stressed vowel's rise. Per segment three cards in (kind, s, n); per frame u (INP gu) and the pitch so far (INP
; gb); per frame the pitch out. In a vowel with stress 1 (or 2) the pitch rises by r0 = 15 (or 7) percent of it at
; the vowel's start, falling off to 40 percent of that at its end: + r0 - r0 6 u / 100. r0 is b f / 100 by Horner
; over f's two digits; each product is a jump into the row of nine ADD y (90-98), which runs into 99 and back.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            seg     INP   kind     03-09: a segment (i counts its frames down)
  04                    INP   s
  05                    INP   i
  06            frm     CLA   i
  07                    SUB   00
  08                    TAC   seg
  09                    STO   i
  10            gu      INP   u        10-24: a frame: is it a stressed vowel's
  11            gb      INP   b
  12                    CLA   kind
  13                    SUB   n2
  14                    TAC   v
  15                    JMP   out
  16            v       CLA   s
  17                    SUB   00
  18                    TAC   out
  19                    SUB   00
  20                    TAC   r15
  21                    CLA   c7
  22                    JMP   rr
  23            r15     CLA   c15
  24            rr      STO   f
  25                    CLA   b        25-46: r0 = b f / 100
  26                    STO   y
  27                    CLA   f
  28                    SFT   33
  29                    STO   d
  30                    CLA   cj
  31                    SUB   d
  32                    STO   j1
  33                    CLA   z
  34            j1      DATA  0        (JMP 99-c)
  35                    SFT   01
  36                    STO   t
  37                    CLA   f
  38                    SFT   23
  39                    STO   d
  40                    CLA   cj
  41                    SUB   d
  42                    STO   j2
  43                    CLA   t
  44            j2      DATA  0        (JMP 99-b)
  45                    SFT   01
  46                    STO   r0
  47                    STO   y        47-66: r0 u, then 6 times that, / 100
  48                    CLA   cj
  49                    SUB   u
  50                    STO   j3
  51                    CLA   z
  52            j3      DATA  0        (JMP 99-u)
  53                    STO   y
  54                    CLA   cj
  55                    SUB   six
  56                    STO   j4
  57                    CLA   z
  58            j4      DATA  0        (JMP 93)
  59                    SFT   02
  60                    STO   t
  61                    CLA   b
  62                    ADD   r0
  63                    SUB   t
  64                    STO   b
  65            out     OUT   b
  66                    JMP   frm
  70            kind    DATA  0
  71            s       DATA  0
  72            i       DATA  0
  73            u       DATA  0
  74            b       DATA  0
  75            f       DATA  0
  76            y       DATA  0
  77            d       DATA  0
  78            t       DATA  0
  79            r0      DATA  0
  80            z       DATA  0
  81            n2      DATA  2
  82            c7      DATA  7
  83            c15     DATA  15
  84            six     DATA  6
  85            cj      JMP   99
  90            row     ADD   y        90-98: the row of nine ADD y, into 99
  91                    ADD   y
  92                    ADD   y
  93                    ADD   y
  94                    ADD   y
  95                    ADD   y
  96                    ADD   y
  97                    ADD   y
  98                    ADD   y
